  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIf one submits a form and does a window stop in the same task, then following the wording of [To stop loading a navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#navigable) results in the planned form navigation going through; this is because the [planned form navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#planned-navigation) is a an element task, so it is not one of the fetch task cancelled as part of `nav-stop`, and the navigation is started in a subsequent task, so the setting of the `ongoing navigation` to `null` in the current task, so before the subsequent task has run, does not affect the navigation of the form. \n\nI tested the behavior of FF and Safari, and both would cancel the navigation, so it seems the spec is wrong? \n\nI have written a test over at https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/54325",
